WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.042
A query can contain several common table expressions, and later stages can use results produced by earlier stages.

00:00:08.042 --> 00:00:10.807
Think of this as a small pipeline.

00:00:10.807 --> 00:00:14.082
The first stage may calculate admission counts.

00:00:14.082 --> 00:00:18.187
The second stage may join those counts to patient information.

00:00:18.187 --> 00:00:23.095
The final stage may create a label such as repeat visitor or single visit.

00:00:23.738 --> 00:00:28.595
This structure is useful because every stage has one clear responsibility.

00:00:28.595 --> 00:00:35.589
When a result looks wrong, you can inspect one stage at a time instead of debugging one very large query.
